I am not sure how mouse events are handled while dragging, but IIRC, if you start dragging on a given control, this control will keep receiving MouseMotion events even if you drag outside of it. If that's the case as I think it is, I think your fix only needs a few changes to be good.

To do so you should replicate and adapt those lines from `_tile_atlas_control_gui_input` into `_tile_alternatives_control_gui_input`: 
```
else if (drag_type == DRAG_TYPE_MAY_POPUP_MENU) {
				if (Vector2(drag_start_mouse_pos).distance_to(tile_atlas_control->get_local_mouse_position()) > 5.0 * EDSCALE) {
					drag_type = DRAG_TYPE_NONE;
				}
			} 
```
